35,2,1,talk,Servas,,"The audit is a nightmare. Hardware needs outside appraisal, adding six weeks and fees.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Asuka,,The data is clear. Back-office tooling for finance sold well. The write-off ran its own premises.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minako,,The reserve is thin. The credit line ignores subscription contracts. We are borrowing against air.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Recruiters fill support roles fast, but field crews take four months. The advisers are idle.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Toshio,,Security reviews for medical data take three quarters. Hardware devices lost five months to shortages.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Minako, your concern is valid. The appraisal fees are a silent tax on our quarter-end.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Toshio, that delay is critical. If we pick a company with heavy compliance, we are stuck.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Servas, I agree. We cannot afford the appraisal fees if the credit line is already stretched.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Asuka, the write-off is a warning. We must avoid companies that need physical premises.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Mio, the field crew delay is a red flag. We need a team that doesn't rely on seasonal labor.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@Asuka, the back-office tooling is the safest bet. It avoids the hardware appraisal trap.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Servas, precisely. The retention data shows financial tools keep customers. We should follow that path.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Toshio, the security review delay is a dealbreaker for medical data. We must avoid that risk.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Minako, I agree. The credit line terms mean we can't support long-term hardware investments.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Mio, the delivery records show software inside a bank cycle never missed a release. That is stability.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Servas,,The evidence points to software that integrates with existing financial systems. It is the only path.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Asuka,,I concur. The exits and retention data favor financial operations tooling. Let us choose wisely.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Minako,,I agree. The financial reality supports a software-only model. We must respect the budget.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Mio,,I’m glad we’re all looking at different angles. I’ll stick with my two choices to understand the staffing.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Toshio,,I will weigh the candidates against the delivery evidence to ensure we fund what actually endures.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
